# A fixture is driven by a real `spec-test` sub-run, so the runner makes its usual scratch here:
# `.spec-tmp/` (already ignored repo-wide) and a `fragments/<target>/` tree. Nothing lands in the
# latter while the refusals hold — a case that FAILS never reaches the golden write — so a `.test`
# appearing here means a refusal stopped firing, which the self-test itself reports far more loudly.
# Ignored so a neutered-refusal experiment cannot leave a committed artefact behind.
fragments/
